//! Mirrors what happens when an exception escapes `main` in a libstdc++ program.
//!
//! The C++ original never catches anything, so `std::stoi` failures (and the `std::logic_error`
//! from constructing a `std::string` out of the NULL `argv[argc]`) propagate out of `main`,
//! where the default `std::terminate` handler prints
//!
//! ```text
//! terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::invalid_argument'
//!   what():  stoi
//! ```
//!
